    {
      "key": "withdrawal",
      "name": "Secondary off",
      "expected": "Every link to CHR 2 loses carrier at once, as on a real power loss. CHR 1 (MLAG primary) sees its peer port ether2 go down and keeps the shared system ID, so the access switch's uplink bond and traffic host 2 keep their LACP partner. They drop their member to CHR 2 on carrier loss, without waiting for the LACP short timeout, and forward over their members to CHR 1. With protocol-mode=none no port changes state and no BPDUs appear.",
      "source": "https://manual.mikrotik.com/docs/high-availability-solutions/multi-chassis-link-aggregation-group/",
